diff --git a/docs/requirements.rst b/docs/requirements.rst
index fede671..eab5b10 100644
--- a/docs/requirements.rst
+++ b/docs/requirements.rst
@@ -72,6 +72,22 @@ Usage
 Reference
 ---------
 
+Use :meth:`Requirement.__replace__` to copy a requirement with selected fields
+changed. It accepts the keyword arguments ``name``, ``url``, ``extras``,
+``specifier`` and ``marker``, using the same types as the attributes. Omitted
+fields are preserved, and the original is unchanged. Invalid values or values
+that would parse into different fields raise :class:`InvalidRequirement`.
+Specifier sets and their specifiers are copied with their prerelease settings.
+
+.. doctest::
+
+    >>> req = Requirement('requests[security]>=2; python_version >= "3"')
+    >>> req.__replace__(name="flask")
+    <Requirement('flask[security]>=2; python_version >= "3"')>
+
+On Python 3.13 and later, this also works with :func:`copy.replace`.
+
 .. automodule:: packaging.requirements
     :members:
+    :special-members: __replace__
     :exclude-members: __init__, __new__
